{"blocks":[["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-4926","Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-encode-garden is an unusually good first corpus: GitHub currently indexes approximately 4,968 Markdown files under pages/ and 507 under journals/, about 5,475 Markdown page/journal files total, and code search finds id:: in 318 Markdown files. It is therefore large enough to make caching and incremental behavior real engineering concerns rather than speculative architecture.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Executive summary"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5348","Repository landscape",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5375","Relevance abbreviations: Core = parser/index/semantic core; Editor = LSP/Neovim; Publish = static/publishing; Bench = useful corpus/performance precedent; CLI = humans/agents/scripts.",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5583","lsdoc (P0)",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5602","Priority: P0",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","lsdoc (P0)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5620","URL: martinkoutecky/lsdoc",["Logseq-Gardener Ecosystem Research Brief","Repository landscape","lsdoc (P0)"]],["Person/codekiln/GitHub/logseq-gardener/Project/Research/26/09/relevant%20repo%20precedents/","source-block-5694","Language / license / status: Rust; AGPL-3.0. Created June 2026, pushed Sept. 1, 2026; young bu